WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.880
Saudi Arabia's government is spending $80 billion to remodel Mecca

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.100
including $3.5 billion to build the largest hotel in the world

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.100
Why is Mecca having a dramatic makeover?

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:21.100
Mecca is the home of Islam's holiest site - the Kaaba, within the Grand Mosque

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:26.600
Around eight million Muslims made pilgrimage to the city in 2016

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:32.920
Visitors peak during the week of the Hajj

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:39.300
During the pilgrimage an extra two million people cram into the city

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.720
Making it the largest annual gathering in the world

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.960
Religious tourism is crucial to the Saudi economy

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:54.980
It's the Kingdom's third-highest source of income after oil and petrochemicals

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:01.000
But oil revenues are faltering and the budget deficit exploded

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:06.720
So the government is trying to boost tourism to help plug the gap

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:12.100
The goal: An extra 20 million annual visitors to Mecca by 2030

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:17.420
The Grand Mosque is already the largest in the world

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:21.860
In 2016, around $10 billion was budgeted for the work

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:26.460
By 2040, capacity will be doubled to nearly seven million worshippers at any one time

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:29.760
Pilgrims will be accommodated in the biggest hotel in the world

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.800
With 10,000 rooms

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.380
And 70 restaurants

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:41.640
As part of the redevelopment, 13 of Mecca's 15 old neighbourhoods have been razed and rebuilt

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.700
Of the city's scores of old shrines, only the Kaaba survives

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:55.380
Saudi authorities are banking on the redevelopment attracting more pilgrims, and more money, into the economy

